## llvm-cil-dump --canonical (plan 5.7.10, canonical listing v1): the header
## lines, every type with its layout, interfaces, custom attributes, fields
## (offsets, constants, marshalling, FieldRVA data of known and unknown size),
## properties and methods (P/Invoke, parameters, bodies with every operand
## kind, EH clauses of every kind), the trailer; names quoted and escaped,
## sorted by UTF-8 bytes. The expected listing is mdcanon's (M16) for the same
## image, reviewed against 5.7.10; both dumpers must print it byte for byte.
## The input is a yaml2obj copy of the ilasm (.NET Framework 4.8, -dll -pe64
## -x64) image of canon.il.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# RUN: yaml2obj %t/canon.yaml -o %t/canon.dll

## --canonical is the default mode, and the defaults are --scopes=keep,
## --order=sorted, --forms=exact and keep for the six 5.12.6 options.
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump %t/canon.dll > %t/default.txt
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --canonical %t/canon.dll > %t/canonical.txt
# RUN: diff %t/default.txt %t/canonical.txt
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump --canonical --scopes=keep --order=sorted --forms=exact \
# RUN:   --assembly-hash=keep --params=keep --initlocals=keep --snan=keep \
# RUN:   --pinvoke-module=keep --pinvoke-access=keep %t/canon.dll > %t/keep.txt
# RUN: diff %t/default.txt %t/keep.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/canonical.txt --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

